WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.008
- You were in like a horrific accident.

00:00:02.008 --> 00:00:02.841
- Mmhmm.

00:00:02.841 --> 00:00:04.300
- When you were a kid. At
it was a truck hit you.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.440
- Cement truck.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.273
- A big cement truck.

00:00:06.273 --> 00:00:07.780
- A bigger kind of truck.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.824
- Dang! Not even like an F-150.

00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:14.250
- Not a little, not an
F-150, not an F-250, bigger.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.270
- How did that shape you?

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.160
Because you've gotta be...

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.353
- Mangled me.

00:00:18.353 --> 00:00:19.690
(audience laughing)

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.819
I was a very weird shape after that.

00:00:21.819 --> 00:00:23.297
(laughing)

00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:24.293
Obtuse?

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.440
- All the geometric angles.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.338
- A lot of weird angles.

00:00:29.338 --> 00:00:31.527
- No, I mean, not physically.

00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:32.789
(laughing)

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:35.229
I meant mentally and emotionally.

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:36.062
- Yeah.

00:00:36.062 --> 00:00:37.640
- That had to kind of change things.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.473
You're funny.

00:00:38.473 --> 00:00:39.691
- For sure.

00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:40.524
(laughing)

00:00:40.524 --> 00:00:42.883
Well, no absolutely. I think,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.978
now I'm happy that it happened

00:00:48.978 --> 00:00:49.811
- Yeah.

00:00:49.811 --> 00:00:51.590
- Because I don't think I'd
be doing what I'm doing.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:55.528
And it also, it gave me the confidence,

00:00:55.528 --> 00:00:58.070
because I had to re-learn how to walk

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.560
and I couldn't walk, it
was a two year process

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.350
to gain the strength back in my legs

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.560
and learn how to walk again

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.530
and I lost all of the muscle

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.910
and I shattered everything
from my knees down

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.590
and so I had to fully re-learn,

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.859
and that's really hard to do, turns out.

00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:13.880
- Turns out.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:14.713
(laughing)

00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:17.460
- You think, on paper, yeah,
one step, another step,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.659
you got it.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:21.069
You figured it out when you were one,

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:22.499
you can figure it out now.

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:23.360
- Oh my God.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.070
- It was very hard. And so now
"I'm like I can do anything"

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.028
when I can't.

00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:29.967
But I have that confidence.

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:33.300
- I think that a lot of creative people

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.160
have odd things that happen to them

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.570
either horrible or whatever

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:37.420
cause it kind shapes you

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.640
and it makes you this creative person.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.570
You can, you know, make fun of yourself

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.688
like self deprecation.

00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:42.521
- For sure.

00:01:42.521 --> 00:01:44.707
- And even have no shame,
you're just like "I'm in it!"

